DESCRIPTION:Sunday May 10th\, 2026 from 10:00am - 12:00pm Location: 1688 Q
 ueen Street West *Price is per person light refreshments included. Celebra
 te Mother’s Day with a creative\, hands-on experience inspired by the be
 auty of spring. Guests will learn how to press delicate flower stems into 
 clay\, capturing organic textures and transforming them into timeless mugs
  and dishes—each piece uniquely shaped by hand and nature. You’ll be g
 uided through the hand-building process before selecting from a curated pa
 lette of specialty glazes to finish your work with a refined\, personal to
 uch. To complete the experience\, each guest will receive a handmade bud v
 ase to take home the day of—perfect for displaying fresh blooms. Four we
 eks later\, your finished pieces will be ready for pickup\, serving as tan
 gible reminders of the wonderful experience you shared. Suitable for begin
 ners and beyond\, this workshop welcomes all skill levels. No prior experi
 ence is necessary\; just bring your creativity and enthusiasm! Additional 
 Info: The last 15-20 minutes of the workshop are designated for cleanup. R
 emember to bring an apron and good vibes! Please note that we do not offer
  refunds! This is a one time special event so there won't be an option to 
 reschedule either. Please ensure that you can make the date!
