BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mold-Making 101 with Janet Macpherson | 2 Weekends
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260425T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260425T160000
UID:parkdale-9903312994587@parkdalepottery.ca
DESCRIPTION:Dates : Saturday and Sunday April 25-26 & May 2-3\, 2026 Times
  : 10:00am - 4:00pm Location : 300 Campbell Avenue\, Unit 115 Instructor :
  Janet Macpherson Unlock new creative possibilities in ceramics with our c
 omprehensive Mold-Making 101 course. This hands-on class will guide you th
 rough the process of designing and creating plaster molds for both slip ca
 sting and press molding techniques. You’ll learn how to craft one-part a
 nd two-part molds\, make decorative sprig molds\, and combine slip-cast pi
 eces into finished ceramic forms. This course is best for those with some 
 hand-building experience. Throughout the course\, you'll explore: - The fu
 ndamentals of plaster and its use in mold-making. - Techniques for creatin
 g and using press molds and sprig molds. - How to design and construct two
 -part molds for more complex shapes. - The basics of slip casting and asse
 mbling multi-part pieces. - Finishing techniques to prepare your work for 
 firing and glazing. What you'll take home: - Your Molds of course! - 1 - 3
  Slip cast pieces of each mold you complete Please note: 1) Glazing is not
  part of this course. You can book a glazing session seperately ($50) by e
 mailing the technician at our Dupont Location. Glazing sessions include th
 e use of our studio glazes. Firing fee is included. 2) Due to the hands-on
  and cumulative nature of this course\, it's important to attend each sess
 ion as we may not be able to repeat material covered in a missed class in 
 a thorough way although we will try to catch you up. 3) By the end of the 
 course\, you'll have developed a new set of skills\, a collection of uniqu
 e molds\, and the confidence to continue exploring mold-making in your own
  creative practice. ALL WORKSHOPS ARE NON REFUNDABLE
LOCATION:300 Campbell Avenue\, Unit 115\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://parkdalepottery.ca/products/mold-making-101
X-SOURCE:Parkdale Pottery
